      "worked": "Let the digits be $a,b,c,d$, with $a\\ne0$, and let $S$ be the sum of the original number and the rotated number.\n$$\\begin{align*}S&=(1000a+100b+10c+d)+(1000b+100c+10d+a)\\\\S&=1001a+1100b+110c+11d\\\\S&=11(91a+100b+10c+d).\\end{align*}$$\nSince $91a+100b+10c+d$ is an integer, the sum is a multiple of 11.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
